From ee730e1efa164b0c69e55e79fbe74de0f5d84fc8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: khunmax2 <khuncharoenmax1@hotmail.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 16:54:38 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(maic): remove the Chinese defaults a UAT found, and
 de-brand the host frame
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Clicking every control and walking a course end to end, with the sweep done
mechanically: every route fetched and scanned, every visible button clicked with
real pointer events and the resulting DOM scanned, all 1,699 t() calls checked
against both locale tables.

The microphone toast was the thread. Denying permission printed
"无法访问麦克风，请检查权限设置" in every language — the symptom reported days ago.
use-audio-recorder.ts held nine hardcoded Chinese messages; all nine now go
through t() in 13 languages.

Pulling it found the root: defaultLocale was zh-CN, and lib/i18n/config.ts hands
that value to i18next as BOTH lng and fallbackLng. The first paint was Chinese,
and any key missing from a locale fell back to Chinese rather than English. Now
en-US.

Four more of the same shape:
- Azure SSML hardcoded xml:lang='zh-CN' on both <speak> and <voice>, so Azure
  read every language with Chinese phonetics. An Azure voice is named for its
  locale (th-TH-PremwadeeNeural), so the tag now comes from the voice id.
- asr-settings.tsx and use-browser-asr.ts fell back to zh-CN for browser speech
  recognition; use-browser-tts.ts did the same for synthesis, plus its own
  Chinese error string.
- pbl/v2/submission.tsx looked receipts up under zh-CN.
- components/agent/agent-config-panel.tsx — 11 Chinese strings, imported by
  nothing — deleted.

stage.proMode was called by header-controls.tsx and defined in no locale, so the
label beside the Pro switch rendered the literal key. Upstream's gate compares
locales against each other and never checks that a t() call resolves. Added in 13
languages, with the six classroom transport controls whose aria-labels were
hardcoded English beside translated neighbours.

The host's own frame was still branded: the panel header, the new-tab tooltip,
the iframe's accessible name, the sidebar tooltip and the voice widget all named
OpenMAIC. Reworded in en/th/zh, and /maic is now /course-studio with a 308
redirect.

Verified: a Thai prompt produced a Thai course throughout with no language
mixing, no server errors, and every route scans 0 brand / 0 external links / 0
raw keys. tsc clean, eslint clean, i18n gate at 13 locales, DeepTutor node tests
1105/1105.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
